{"id":"7ce5836b707a87d9","group":"58","path":"58/batch19/58-thm-shoenfield-absoluteness.md","title":"Shoenfield Absoluteness","display":"thm-shoenfield-absoluteness — Shoenfield Absoluteness","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-shoenfield-absoluteness","aliases":["58-thm-shoenfield-absoluteness","Shoenfield Absoluteness Theorem"],"display":"thm-shoenfield-absoluteness — Shoenfield Absoluteness","depends_on":["[[58-df-zfc-transitive-model]]","[[58-df-satisfaction]]","[[58-df-formula]]","[[58-df-proper]]","[[58-df-assignment]]","[[58-df-structure]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-shoenfield-absoluteness"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-shoenfield-absoluteness</span><span>Shoenfield Absoluteness Theorem</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-shoenfield-absoluteness — Shoenfield Absoluteness"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"a9132c2c1a18acd1\" href=\"?note=a9132c2c1a18acd1\" title=\"58-df-zfc-transitive-model\">58-df-zfc-transitive-model</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"58-df-satisfaction\">58-df-satisfaction</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"58-df-formula\">58-df-formula</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"8935dcac821c0104\" href=\"?note=8935dcac821c0104\" title=\"58-df-proper\">58-df-proper</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"64f35ba2e87964e0\" href=\"?note=64f35ba2e87964e0\" title=\"58-df-assignment\">58-df-assignment</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"d9b8711cda3f31ca\" href=\"?note=d9b8711cda3f31ca\" title=\"58-df-structure\">58-df-structure</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Explicit relation signatures used below: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MembershipTruth}_S\\subseteq V^{3}\">\\(\\mathrm{MembershipTruth}_S\\subseteq V^{3}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\\subseteq V^{4}\">\\(\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\\subseteq V^{4}\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TransitiveModel}_S\\subseteq V^{1}\">\\(\\mathrm{TransitiveModel}_S\\subseteq V^{1}\\)</span>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M,N,r,\\varphi^{\\mathrm{set}}\\in V\">\\(M,N,r,\\varphi^{\\mathrm{set}}\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{TransitiveModel}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{TransitiveModel}_S\\)</span> is the canonical ZFC transitive-model predicate</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"r\\in\\mathbb R\\cap M\">\\(r\\in\\mathbb R\\cap M\\)</span></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi(v_0)\">\\(\\varphi(v_0)\\)</span> is a fixed metatheoretic lightface <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma^1_2\">\\(\\Sigma^1_2\\)</span> or <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Pi^1_2\">\\(\\Pi^1_2\\)</span> formula and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi^{\\mathrm{set}}(v_0)\">\\(\\varphi^{\\mathrm{set}}(v_0)\\)</span> is its canonical membership-language translation</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L_{\\in}\">\\(\\mathcal L_{\\in}\\)</span> is the set code for the pure membership language imported from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"8935dcac821c0104\" href=\"?note=8935dcac821c0104\" title=\"58-df-proper\">58-df-proper</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Assign}\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\mathrm{Assign}\\subseteq V^2\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Univ}:V\\to V\">\\(\\mathrm{Univ}:V\\to V\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I^{(-)}_{\\mathrm{rel},2}\">\\(I^{(-)}_{\\mathrm{rel},2}\\)</span> are the imported assignment, carrier, and binary-relation interpretation operations (with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{rel}\">\\(\\mathrm{rel}\\)</span> the relation-sort tag)</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{MembershipTruth}_S(A,\\psi,a)\">\\(\\mathrm{MembershipTruth}_S(A,\\psi,a)\\)</span> is the set-model truth predicate defined below from actual satisfaction data</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}membership\\text{-}truth}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{MembershipTruth}_S(A,\\psi,a)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists\\mathfrak A,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat},s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(&amp;\n\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathfrak A)=A\n\\land\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(\\mathfrak A,\\mathcal L_{\\in},\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\\\\\n&amp;\\land I^{\\mathfrak A}_{\\mathrm{rel},2}(\\dot\\in)\n=\\{\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in A^2:x\\in y\\}\n\\land\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathfrak A,s)\\\\\n&amp;\\land s(v_0)=a\\land\\operatorname{Sat}(\\psi,s)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}membership\\text{-}truth}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{MembershipTruth}_S(A,\\psi,a)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists\\mathfrak A,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat},s\\in V\\;\\Bigl(&amp;\n\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathfrak A)=A\n\\land\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(\\mathfrak A,\\mathcal L_{\\in},\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\\\\\n&amp;\\land I^{\\mathfrak A}_{\\mathrm{rel},2}(\\dot\\in)\n=\\{\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in A^2:x\\in y\\}\n\\land\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathfrak A,s)\\\\\n&amp;\\land s(v_0)=a\\land\\operatorname{Sat}(\\psi,s)\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}shoenfield\\text{-}absoluteness}[\\varphi]\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{TransitiveModel}_S(M)\\land\\mathrm{TransitiveModel}_S(N)\n\\land M\\subseteq N\\land\\omega_1^N\\in M\n\\land r\\in\\mathbb R\\cap M\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{MembershipTruth}_S(M,\\varphi^{\\mathrm{set}},r)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{MembershipTruth}_S(N,\\varphi^{\\mathrm{set}},r)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}shoenfield\\text{-}absoluteness}[\\varphi]\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{TransitiveModel}_S(M)\\land\\mathrm{TransitiveModel}_S(N)\n\\land M\\subseteq N\\land\\omega_1^N\\in M\n\\land r\\in\\mathbb R\\cap M\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\Bigl(\n\\mathrm{MembershipTruth}_S(M,\\varphi^{\\mathrm{set}},r)\n\\leftrightarrow\n\\mathrm{MembershipTruth}_S(N,\\varphi^{\\mathrm{set}},r)\n\\Bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Shoenfield (1961): fundamental absoluteness theorem.</li>\n<li>Lower level (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_1^1\">\\(\\Sigma_1^1\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Pi_1^1\">\\(\\Pi_1^1\\)</span>) statements are also absolute (Mostowski absoluteness).</li>\n<li>Higher levels (<span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\Sigma_3^1\">\\(\\Sigma_3^1\\)</span> and above) are NOT absolute in general.</li>\n<li>The assertion is a theorem schema indexed externally by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\varphi\">\\(\\varphi\\)</span>; the complexity test is therefore not confused with an unregistered object-language predicate.  Since <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span> is transitive, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega_1^N\\in M\">\\(\\omega_1^N\\in M\\)</span> entails that every ordinal below <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega_1^N\">\\(\\omega_1^N\\)</span> lies in <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Both truth values are evaluated in set-coded membership structures.  The ambient proper class <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span> is never supplied where the satisfaction definition requires a set-coded structure.</li>\n<li>A key application is absoluteness between <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"L\">\\(L\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V\">\\(V\\)</span> at this complexity level.</li>\n<li>Key tool in descriptive set theory and forcing analysis.</li>\n<li>The comparison requires the smaller model to contain the larger model's <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega_1\">\\(\\omega_1\\)</span>; without enough ordinals this formulation does not apply.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-zfc-transitive-model","status":"resolved","id":"a9132c2c1a18acd1","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-zfc-transitive-model]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-satisfaction","status":"resolved","id":"8b6a90316aad78a4","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-satisfaction]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-formula","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-formula]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-proper","status":"resolved","id":"8935dcac821c0104","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-proper]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-assignment","status":"resolved","id":"64f35ba2e87964e0","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnc